 "doc": {
  "source_notes": "D:\\Blender\\blender-mcp\\Projects\\Cat In Hat\\STL\\FinalSTL\\Cat in the Hat Hot Air Balloon - Assembly Instructions.txt",
  "cover": {
   "image": "D:\\gimp-mcp\\Projects\\CatInHat\\Drafts\\RealImages\\Better Pictures\\20261029_105731_logo.png",
   "title": "CAT IN THE HAT",
   "subtitle": "Hot Air Balloon"
  },
  "blocks": [
   {
    "h1": "Before You Start"
   },
   {
    "p": "A striped-hat hot air balloon with the red flying couch hanging below it, held up by three clouds behind it. Every part prints separately and is glued together. The clouds carry all the weight. The strings are only for looks."
   },
   {
    "callout": {
     "title": "Left / right",
     "lines": [
      "in these instructions = as seen from the FRONT of the couch."
     ],
     "style": "info"
    }
   },
   {
    "callout": {
     "title": "Before you glue:",
     "lines": [
      "Dry fit every joint first. Super glue grabs fast, so make sure each part goes in the right way before any glue goes on."
     ],
     "style": "info"
    }
   },
   {
    "h2": "What you need"
   },
   {
    "bullets": [
     "The printed parts (see Printing below)",
     "Gold PLA filament, 1.75 mm (the same gold used for the levers and bracket), for the strings and control shafts. ~~Optional: 1/16 in brass rod instead of filament for the control shafts (Hobby Lobby carries it). Brass is NOT required. Gold filament looks great and is what the parts are designed around.~~",
     "Super glue (CA glue)",
     "Flush cutters or a hobby knife, a ruler with mm markings",
     "Hair dryer or heat gun on low (to bend the steering column)"
    ]
   },
   {
    "h2": "Printing"
   },
   {
    "p": "Plates in the 3MF (Bambu PLA Basic, 0.4 nozzle unless noted):"
   },
   {
    "table": {
     "head": [
      "Plate",
      "Part",
      "Color"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       1,
       "06 Ring 5 (bottom stripe)",
       "Red"
      ],
      [
       2,
       "07 Ring 4",
       "White"
      ],
      [
       3,
       "08 Ring 3",
       "Red"
      ],
      [
       4,
       "09 Ring 2",
       "White"
      ],
      [
       5,
       "10 Top Cap (prints upside down)",
       "Red"
      ],
      [
       6,
       "05 Brim (prints upside down)",
       "White"
      ],
      [
       7,
       "02 Couch",
       "Red"
      ],
      [
       8,
       "11 Bracket",
       "Gold"
      ],
      [
       9,
       "01 Base Cloud",
       "White"
      ],
      [
       10,
       "03 Mid Cloud + 04 Top Cloud",
       "White"
      ],
      [
       11,
       "Wheel, levers, pedals, knobs",
       "Gold + Silver"
      ],
      [
       12,
       "2 dark knobs",
       "Dark brown"
      ]
     ],
     "widths": [
      1100,
      5560,
      2700
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "callout": {
     "title": "IMPORTANT:",
     "lines": [
      "Plates 11 and 12 are labeled “Print with .2 Nozzle”. These parts are tiny. Switch to a 0.2 mm nozzle in Bambu Studio (and on the printer) before slicing those two plates, or they will not print cleanly."
     ],
     "style": "warn"
    }
   },
   {
    "p": "All settings (seams, layer heights, supports, brims) are already saved per part in the 3MF. Just slice and print."
   },
   {
    "h1": "Step 1 – Build the Hat"
   },
   {
    "steps": [
     "**Brim + Ring 5: **The brim has a groove on top with a solid key block at the back. Ring 5 has a bead on its bottom with a gap in it. Line the gap up with the key block and press Ring 5 into the groove. It is a press fit; glue is optional.",
     "**Stack the rings in order: **Ring 5 → Ring 4 → Ring 3 → Ring 2 → Top Cap. Each lower ring has a lip that slides up inside the ring above it. A key rib at the back fits a notch, so each ring only goes on one way. Ring 4 has a small nub on the outside. It must face the **BACK** (it lines up with the top cloud later).",
     "**Glue **each ring joint once the stack fits. Keep the key ribs lined up so the stripes stay straight."
    ]
   },
   {
